m>Last updated November 14, 2026.</em></p><p><strong>New Jersey law sets out when a person occupying land can claim title by adverse possession, and how an owner can remove someone who has no right to be there.</strong></p><h2>What the official sources say</h2><ul><li>30 years&#x27; actual possession of real estate (other than woodlands or uncultivated tracts), uninterruptedly continued by occupancy, descent, conveyance or otherwise, vests full title in the possessor and bars recovery actions, however the possession began. (N.J.S.A. 2A:14-30; <a href='https://lis.njleg.state.nj.us/nxt/gateway.dll/statutes%2F1%2F112%2F342' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>60 years&#x27; actual possession is required for woodlands or uncultivated tracts. (N.J.S.A. 2A:14-30; <a href='https://lis.njleg.state.nj.us/nxt/gateway.dll/statutes%2F1%2F112%2F342' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li></ul><div class=\"chb-cta\" style=\"margin:32px 0;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0F1C2E 0%,#16293F 100%);padding:28px 32px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#fff;\"><div style=\"max-width:600px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:2px;color:#E0A83C;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:6px;\">Selling in New Jersey?</div><div style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:20px;line-height:1.35;color:#fff;\">We buy New Jersey houses as-is, with no commission, no repairs and no closing costs to you.</div></div><a href=\"#\" onclick=\"var f=document.querySelector('iframe[data-form-id]');if(f){f.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});return false;}\" style=\"flex-shrink:0;padding:14px 24px;border-radius:8px;background:#E0A83C;color:#16203A;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;\">Get My Cash Offer &rarr;</a></div><h2>New Jersey Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession FAQ</h2><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Can a squatter take ownership of my New Jersey house?</h3><p> Check the statute and talk to a New Jersey attorney about your facts.</p><div class='wsp-related'><div class='wsp-related-grid'><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/new-jersey-landlord-tenant-law-tenant-rights/'>New Jersey Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/new-jersey-eviction-notice/'>New Jersey Eviction Notice: Types and Days</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/new-jersey-guides-by-city-and-county/'>New Jersey guides by city and county</a><p>Every local guide we publish.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-new-jersey/'>We buy houses in New Jersey</a><p>How a cash offer works.</p></div></div></div><h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href='https://lis.njleg.state.nj.us/nxt/gateway.dll/statutes%2F1%2F112%2F342' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>N.J.S.A. 2A:14-30</a></li></ul><p><em>General information for New Jersey Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession, not legal or tax advice. Confirm details with the official office or a licensed professional.</em></p><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"FAQPage\", \"mainEntity\": [{\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Can a squatter take ownership of my New Jersey house?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Only by meeting every requirement of the adverse possession statute cited above for the full period. Check the statute and talk to a New Jersey attorney about your facts.\"}}]}</script><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/\"}, {\"@ty