x-width:900px){.wsp-hero-inner{grid-template-columns:1fr;}.wsp-hero-left h1{font-size:2.1rem;}}.wsp-wrap h3{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:4px solid #3182CE;border-radius:8px;padding:.9rem 1.25rem;margin:1.75rem 0 0;font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:700;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-wrap h3+p{background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-top:none;border-radius:0 0 8px 8px;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin:0 0 .25rem;color:#444;}.wsp-wrap table td{vertical-align:top;}.chb-cta p{margin:0}.wsp-related{margin:2.5rem 0 1rem}.wsp-related h2{font-size:1.3rem;margin-bottom:1rem;font-weight:600;}.wsp-related-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(220px,1fr));gap:1rem;}.wsp-related-card{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:8px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;}.wsp-related-card a{font-weight:700;color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);text-decoration:none;}.wsp-related-card a:hover{text-decoration:underline;}.wsp-related-card p{margin:.35rem 0 0;font-size:.9rem;color:#555;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call{background:#E0A83C !important;border:2px solid #E0A83C !important;color:#16203A !important;font-size:1.25rem !important;font-weight:800 !important;padding:1rem 2.2rem !important;border-radius:40px !important;box-shadow:0 0 0 4px rgba(224,168,60,.25),0 8px 26px rgba(224,168,60,.5) !important;text-shadow:none !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call strong{color:#16203A !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call:hover{background:#fff !important;border-color:#fff !important;}</style><div class='wsp-hero'><div class='wsp-hero-inner'><div class='wsp-hero-left'><h1>New Jersey Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights: Rules for Selling a Rental</h1><div class=wsp-kicker>Cash Home Buyers in New Jersey</div><div class=wsp-speed><span>Cash Offer in 24 Hours</span></div><ul class=wsp-checks><li>New Jersey Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights: inherited, behind on payments, tenants or repairs, we buy the house as-is</li><li>No fees, commissions or closing costs on a New Jersey Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights sale</li><li>Turn the New Jersey Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights offer down and you owe us nothing</li></ul><h2>Selling a New Jersey House? Get a Cash Offer</h2><p>We buy as-is.</p><p><a class='wsp-btn-outline wsp-btn-call' href='tel:424-435-2326'>Call or Text <strong>&nbsp;(424) 435-2326</strong></a></p></div><div class='wsp-hero-right'><iframe src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/widget/form/zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' data-form-id='zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' title='Cash Offer Form'></iframe><br /><script src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/js/form_embed.js' async></script></div></div></div><div class='wsp-wrap'><p><em>Last updated November 14, 2026.</em></p><p><strong>New Jersey statutes set the basic rules between landlords and tenants, including deposits, notices and what happens when a rental is sold.</strong></p><h2>What the official sources say</h2><ul><li>Annual additional security collected may not exceed 10 percent of the current security deposit. (N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.2 (DCA Security Deposit Law PDF); <a href='https://www.nj.gov/dca/codes/publications/pdf_lti/sdepsit_law.pdf' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Within 30 days after lease termination the owner must return the deposit plus the tenant&#x27;s share of interest, less lawful charges, by personal delivery or registered/certified mail. (N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.1 (DCA Security Deposit Law PDF); <a href='https://www.nj.gov/dca/codes/publications/pdf_lti/sdepsit_law.pdf' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>In a tenant suit for wrongly withheld deposit, the court awards double the amount plus full costs and, in its discretion, reasonable attorney&#x27;s fees. (N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.1; <a href='https://www.nj.gov/dca/codes/publications/pdf_lti/sdepsit_law.pdf' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Landlord may not serve a notice to quit or sue for possession as reprisal for the tenant enforcing lease/legal rights, a good-faith complaint to a government authority about health/safety violations, or tenant organizing; refusing to renew without cause counts as substantial alteration. (N.J.S.A. 2A:42-10.10; <a href='https://nj.gov/dca/codes/publications/pdf_lti/reprisal_law.pdf' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>A notice to quit or substantial change in tenancy without cause after such protected acts creates a rebuttable presumption of reprisal; no presumption arises from non-renewal if the tenant&#x27;s request came sooner than 90 days before lease expiration. (N.J.S.A. 2A:42-10.12; <a href='https://nj.gov/dca/codes/publications/pdf_lti/reprisal_law.pdf' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>A notice to quit is a condition precedent to raising rent in a periodic tenancy (annotation to 2A:18-61.2 citing case law). (DCA annotated N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.1/61.2 PDF; <a href='https://www.nj.gov/dca/codes/codreg/pdf_regs/2A_18_61.pdf' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li></ul><div class=\"chb-cta\" style=\"margin:32px 0;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0F1C2E 0%,#16293F 100%);padding:28px 32px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#fff;\"><div style=\"max-width:600px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:2px;color:#E0A83C;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:6px;\">Selling in New Jersey?</div><div style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:20px;line-height:1.35;color:#fff;\">We buy New Jersey houses as-is, with no commission, no repairs and no closing costs to you.</div></div><a href=\"#\" onclick=\"var f=document.querySelector('iframe[data-form-id]');if(f){f.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});return false;}\" style=\"flex-shrink:0;padding:14px 24px;border-radius:8px;background:#E0A83C;color:#16203A;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;t